  "observedConclusion": "The exact old-source control also reproduces high blocking and JavaScript execution cost under the later measurement conditions. The original after slowdown therefore is not unique to the new product source. Host-condition drift materially confounds the original before/after comparison; these sequential measurements cannot prove a specific host cause or quantify the product-only contribution.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is a later sequential control, not simultaneous randomized A/B sampling. Benchmark drift remains visible within the samples; original poor results are not discarded.",
    "The benchmark index is an observed calibration signal, not direct proof of thermal throttling, driver behavior or a particular competing process. No such cause was measured here.",
    "Lighthouse simulated TBT is not real-device INP. RAF intervals and WebGL call counts are not GPU completion/presentation FPS. Mobile remains desktop-host viewport/touch emulation.",
    "Continuous-script pass flags indicate execution and permissive scroll criteria, not smoothness. Inputs with individually attributed scroll events are reported exactly; original after desktop is 7 of 8 despite eight observed scroll events.",
    "Adaptive shader resolution may differ between samples as an intended response to timing. Actual canvas dimensions are included and have not been normalized after collection."
